        "act1_title": "The first computer in history was born in Europe. Your future must too.",
        "act1_p1": "In the spring of 1901, sponge divers rescued from the bottom of the Aegean Sea, off the small Greek island of Antikythera, a block of corroded bronze that forever changed the history of science. That artifact—designed in the astronomical and mechanical tradition of Archimedes of Syracuse—contained a system of gears capable of calculating with mathematical precision the movement of the cosmos sixteen centuries before any European clock.",
